  "scope": "Actual original-form regular auxiliary primes in the finite linear subfield branch. Nonzero original symmetric twisted classes are detected outside every finite set with original finite affine factor and local Frobenius, retaining all preceding arithmetic and symmetric consequences for the same residual witness.",
  "sourceAssemblyReview": "The final source theorem unpacks the preceding actual-form symmetric/cohomology consumer, keeps its same residual witness and all its conclusions, and derives original regular detecting primes from its constructed finite linear subfield branch. The common finite affine factor is retained in full; the congruence q = 1 modulo p^(level+1) is stronger than the requested p^level congruence. No original class is replaced by a scalar-extended H1 class. Predicate definitions name the literal native statements and do not postulate them. Failed monolithic assemblies and diagnostic variants remain retained; default proof limits are unchanged."
}
